WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
The metals in Group One are a family.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.530
Each one has just a single
electron in its outer shell.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.690
Drop any of them into water and
it fizzes, giving off hydrogen.

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.130
They even make the
same kind of product.

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.430
Yet each metal further down the
group reacts with water more

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.570
violently than the one above it.

7
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.390
If they are so alike, why are
they not equally reactive?

8
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.250
In this mission, you'll learn
how the periodic table is

9
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.510
arranged, and what a group
number tells you about an atom's

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.530
outer electrons.

11
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.030
You'll see what these
metals make with water,

12
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.770
and how their reactivity
changes down the group.

13
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.420
Your mission: explain why
reactivity rises down Group One.
